#kaocha/v1
;; Datomic Pro <-> datahike migration, in its OWN config file.
;;
;; NOT a tier in `tests.edn`, and that is the point: kaocha scans a suite's
;; `:test-paths` off DISK regardless of the classpath, so merely naming
;; `test-datomic` there makes every plain `-M:test` run try to load these
;; namespaces and fail — `datomic.api` exists only under the `:datomic` alias.
;;
;; `:kaocha.testable/skip true` was the first attempt and was worse: kaocha's
;; skip beats `--focus`, so `bb test datomic` ran 0 of 8 tests and said so only
;; in a warning. Silent no-coverage instead of a loud failure.
{:tests [{:id         :datomic
          :test-paths ["test-datomic"]
          :bindings   {datahike.config/*default-index* :datahike.index/persistent-set}}]}
